    "pathway_role_summary": "WNT3A is a prototypical canonical Wnt ligand that initiates β-catenin-dependent signaling. Upon binding to Frizzled receptors and LRP5/6 co-receptors, WNT3A triggers the disassembly of the β-catenin destruction complex (APC/AXIN/GSK3β), leading to β-catenin stabilization, nuclear translocation, and activation of TCF/LEF transcription factors. Critical for embryonic development (mesoderm formation, neural tube patterning, somitogenesis), stem cell self-renewal (intestinal crypts), and implicated in cancer when dysregulated. WNT3A biogenesis requires lipidation by PORCN and trafficking by WLS, making it a key node for therapeutic intervention."
  },
