    "data_quality_notes": "Comprehensive data available from multiple sources. Experimental structures include full-length WNT3A in complex with WLS and receptor complexes. PTM sites well-characterized experimentally (palmitoylation at C77 and S209, glycosylation at N87 and N298). Note: WNT3A shows no clear germline mutation signal but overexpression is common in cancers. PROSITE and SMART domain annotations limited - primary domain classification through InterPro/Pfam. Tissue expression data primarily from Human Protein Atlas and GTEx.",
    "modeling_relevance_summary": "WNT3A is a critical canonical Wnt signaling ligand, essential for modeling Wnt/β-catenin pathway dynamics. Key modeling considerations: (1) Dual lipidation (C77, S209) is absolutely required for activity and secretion - must model PORCN-dependent modification; (2) WLS-dependent trafficking from ER to cell surface - rate-limiting step; (3) Ternary complex formation with FZD and LRP6 - cooperative binding with specific stoichiometry (2:4:2); (4) LRP6 phosphorylation cascade as amplification mechanism; (5) Negative regulation by secreted antagonists (DKK, SFRP); (6) TIKI-mediated cleavage as additional regulatory layer. Structural data supports mechanistic modeling of receptor complex assembly. Extensive interaction data enables construction of complete canonical Wnt pathway network from ligand secretion through β-catenin/TCF transcriptional activation."
  }
}
